DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrccss22lloogg utility generates a change log prefix from RCS files (perhaps
     in the CVS repository) and the ChangeLog (if any).

     The options are as follows:

     --cc _c_h_a_n_g_e_l_o_g
             Output a change log prefix to _c_h_a_n_g_e_l_o_g (default ChangeLog).

     --hh _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e
             Use _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e in change log entries (default current host).

     --ii _i_n_d_e_n_t
             Indent change log lines by _i_n_d_e_n_t spaces (default 8).

     --ll _l_e_n_g_t_h
             Try to limit log lines to _l_e_n_g_t_h characters (default 79).

     --RR      If no _f_i_l_e(s) are given and RCS is used, recurse through working
             directory.

     --rr _o_p_t_i_o_n
             Pass _o_p_t_i_o_n to subsidiary log command.

     --tt _t_a_b_w_i_d_t_h
             Tab stops are every _t_a_b_w_i_d_t_h characters (default 8).

     --uu _l_o_g_i_n_<_T_A_B_>_f_u_l_l_n_a_m_e_<_T_A_B_>_m_a_i_l_a_d_d_r
             Assume _l_o_g_i_n has _f_u_l_l_n_a_m_e and _m_a_i_l_a_d_d_r.

     --vv      Append RCS revision to file names in log lines.

     ----hheellpp  Output help.

     ----vveerrssiioonn
             Output version number.

